Subject: [PATCH] pandora: let Metal open the accelerator with its own type

backboardd opens AGXAccelerator with type 1 and PandoraAdrenoGpu::newUserClient
answers 0xe00002c7, because it only accepts Turnip's 0x4147.  That refusal is
why the compositor never gets a Metal device and the screen tears.

Same change as 0344, written against this tree: here the check still sits in
PandoraAdrenoGpu::newUserClient and there is no 0333 to accept type 0 first.

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/PandoraAdrenoGpu.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/PandoraAdrenoGpu.cpp
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/PandoraAdrenoGpu.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/PandoraAdrenoGpu.cpp
@@ -548,7 +548,12 @@
 PandoraAdrenoGpu::newUserClient(task_t owningTask, void *securityID, UInt32 type,
     __unused OSDictionary *properties, IOUserClient **handler)
 {
-	if (type != PANDORA_GPU_OPEN_TYPE) {
+	/*
+	 * Metal opens the accelerator with type 1, Turnip with 0x4147. Both are the same client;
+	 * accept the small numbers Metal uses and keep the refusal logged.
+	 */
+	if (type != PANDORA_GPU_OPEN_TYPE && type > 8) {
+		IOLog("PANDORA GPU UC: open type %#x refused\n", type);
 		return kIOReturnUnsupported;
 	}
 	int c = pandora_gpu_open();
